WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.680
Hi, I'm Phil from BBC Learning English.

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:05.580
Today, I'm going to tell you five ways

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.779
to use in with time expressions.

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:09.960
Number one: months.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.030
I can say: I'm going on holiday in May.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.420
Number two: seasons.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:20.260
So, we can say: In winter, it's cold.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.820
Number three: years.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.520
So, I can say: I finished school in 2000.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.840
Number four: most times of day.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.780
I leave home in the morning.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.460
I get home in the evening.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:40.300
But, I go to sleep at night.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.070
It's an exception!

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:43.260
Number five.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.440
We use it with in the past, in the present

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.760
and in the future.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:53.720
In the future, you'll learn everything from videos.

